al_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icc1000fd1072bc21c74f4631a093e28175c1a6ad" commit="c7a4f55f49e7b1bb8b936c452e68a6b17f532669" commit_message="station_entry: show a big PASS when all tests are done  Some partners suggest that showing a big &quot;PASS&quot; message help their operators easier to understand that this unit has complete and pass all tests in this station.  BUG=chromium:506788 TEST=manual test  Change-Id: Icc1000fd1072bc21c74f4631a093e28175c1a6ad Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360743 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360743" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/43/360743/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4bf2bb22150b3a153c92aea2a7dcfde9d2684f6b" commit="10f4365e9a28bbcf0acc8cff436b3c6b693c879f" commit_message="Device-Aware API: Change from DUT API to a more general Device API.  The DUT-Aware API works fine for pytests, but we now realized there are more to change for station-based environments - especially in the test controller &quot;Goofy&quot; and test frameworks (for example test list) that needs to deal with different environments, like offline mode or Windows.  The solution is to extend DUT API to a more general namespace that both DUT and station can use. It also needs to live outside 'test' sub folder because many Goofy and core modules will need it, for finding environment settings like location of factory related folders.  Before:   from cros.factory.test import dut   self._dut = dut.Create()  After:   from cros.factory.device import device_utils   self._dut = device_utils.CreateDUTInterface()  And the new approach to specify 