5941" commit="c8dbf579067938f71115fae35732e939fcb9df7d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: dts: Add dts for gale-v2  Update GPIO mapping. Remove Audio. Remove captouch.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55320 TEST=None  Change-Id: I2839189715877b6b28cf8f1163ca0dc0ba6b5941 Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361591 Reviewed-by: Suresh Rajashekara &lt;sureshraj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="361591" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/361591/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I98947f2589a62637dcace2e47094bb056a948e94" commit="3c1a12fb6c0dfb2174e8d355265d107136257144" commit_message="graphics_Gbm: Fix potential segmentation fault  gbm_bo_destroy(bo1) frees the bo, potentially causing a runtime error when we query for the stride.  Reorder code for safety.  TEST=Ran graphics_Gbm with no regressions. BUG=NONE  Change-Id: I98947f2589a62637dcace2e47094bb056a948e94 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361542 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="361542" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/42/361542/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I51fae6bd111cf3ff3c1dfbed7441868abad8fc15" commit="d0d2b1e63c458a34fcad2a038eaf462e975a527b" commit_message="Support 'tpmc setbgloballock' for tpm2 case  Some scripts call 'tpmc setbgloballock' or 'tpmc block'. For tpm2 it should be equivalent to pplock, i.e. perform rollback protection actions: writelock for NVRAM firmware index and disable platform hierarchy.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:55210 TEST=run 'tpmc block' on kevin, check that it attempts pplock  Change-Id: I51fae6bd111cf3ff3c1dfbed7441868abad8fc15 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361381 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="361381" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/81/361381/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I519a445fd1b9b51998c8a388f51d3fe30d34843f" commit="53c6800006cfe3666972a4d5fba67a8b894dc327" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/tegra: Change to use .disable when suspend  .dpms doesn't make much sense for dc suspend, because we have nothing to do for DRM_MODE_DPMS_STANDBY and DRM_MODE_DPMS_SUSPEND.  Also if we follow the DPMS way, userspace is able to use the DPMS APIs which is not what we want.  So this patch makes some change to use .disable when suspend, we loop the in-use encoder and the corresponding crtcs, then disable them.  Change-Id: I519a445fd1b9b51998c8a388f51d3fe30d34843f Signed-off-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360745 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="360745" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/45/360745/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifb72ff5080a4ac5f8d63b5c0713e5bb184f176ca" commit="a5aa3bdb4ab2ae5eb7aed4d305b3a424bdc93813" commit_message="Read NVRAM with proper authorization for tpm2  In TPM2 case, NVRAM must be read with empty password authorization in tpmc, since platform hierarchy is disabled by firmware or trunksd for rollback prevention.  Since all NVRAM indices are now defined with AUTHREAD, switch to empty password authorization from platform authorization for all NVRAM reads in Tlcl.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:55210 BUG=chrome-os-partner:55251 TEST=Run 'initctl stop trunksd; tpmc read 0x1008 0xd&quot; on      kevin, verify that it returns the right output.  Change-Id: Ifb72ff5080a4ac5f8d63b5c0713e5bb184f176ca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360944 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360944" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/44/360944/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="8608.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>